==========================================================================
SECTION 7 — Root cause summary
==========================================================================

Bug location: tool/transient_py/clm_v4_hf_format_shim.py:643

  638  wrapped_state = {f"decoder.{k}": v.contiguous() for k, v in state.items()}
  ...
  643  safetensors_save(wrapped_state, str(out_dir / "model.safetensors"), ...)

The shim KNOWS about weight tying:
  - Line 38 docstring: "dual heads: head_a + head_g, both (64000, 768), tied to tok_emb"
  - Line 354 ConsciousDecoderV3 ctor: tie_word_embeddings=True
  - Lines 451-452: explicit re-tie in set_input_embeddings:
        self.decoder.head_a.weight = self.decoder.tok_emb.weight
  - Line 597 config: "tie_word_embeddings": True

But _save_hf_format() flattens everything into wrapped_state as separate keys
without de-duplicating tied storages, then hands it to safetensors.torch.save_file
which has a strict shared-memory guard (introduced in modern safetensors).

Two correct fix patterns (NEITHER applied — out of BG-Δ scope):
  A) Use HF idiomatic: model.save_pretrained(out_dir, safe_serialization=True)
     — auto-detects ties via _tied_weights_keys and stores only one copy.
  B) Pre-clone before save:
     wrapped_state["decoder.head_a.weight"] = wrapped_state["decoder.tok_emb.weight"].detach().clone()

Plus a SEPARATE concern: param_count -53.3M.
  Loaded: 477,648,512.    Expected: 530,994,816.    Delta: -53,346,304.
  Possible causes (investigation needed):
    - tok_emb tied to head_a counted once in load, twice in expected: 64000*768=49.15M
      → that's close to half the gap (53.3M) but not exact; insufficient explanation.
    - head_g (second head) absent from best.pt — also (64000,768)=49.15M
      → could account for ~most of the gap (49.15 vs 53.35M, ~4M residual).
    - Need to enumerate state_dict keys vs ConsciousDecoderV3.named_parameters() to confirm.

